        tut_jogar:       "Play",
        tut_pagina:      "Page {0} of {1}",
        tut_p1_titulo: "Your mission",
        tut_p1_texto:  "You command a base on Mars. Survive 10 sols (Mars days) and help NASA learn if people can live there. The MISSION card shows your goals: survive, collect regolith samples, find iron, silicon and magnesium, and keep the machines working.",
        tut_p2_titulo: "The 4 bars",
        tut_p2_texto:  "LIFE SUPPORT (air, water and crew health), ENERGY, FOOD and SHIELD (protection against radiation). Each bar starts with 3 of 5 points. If ANY bar reaches ZERO, the mission FAILS!",
        tut_p3_titulo: "Action points",
        tut_p3_texto:  "Each day you have 5 action points (the hand icons). Using a machine costs 1 action point. Mission Control is free. When the points run out, the day ends. Use SKIP THE DAY to end the day early. The points come back every morning.",
        tut_p4_titulo: "Machines",
        tut_p4_texto:  "Click a machine and the nearest astronaut goes to use it. Kilopower: +1 Energy. Water Tanks, CO2 Filter and Beds: +1 Life support. Greenhouse: +1 Food. Science Lab: uses 1 regolith for +1 Shield. If the bar is already full, nothing is spent.",
        tut_p5_titulo: "Broken machines",
        tut_p5_texto:  "Night events can sometimes break a machine. A broken machine stops working (smoke comes out of it). Click it to repair: it uses materials from storage plus 1 action point. Expeditions bring the materials.",
        tut_p6_titulo: "Mars weather",
        tut_p6_texto:  "The Weather Station shows the real weather of today and tomorrow (NASA InSight) and the next night's event. Mission Control shows tomorrow's weather. Cold: 1 extra energy at night. Windy: the Kilopower costs 1 extra action point. Calm: a normal day.",
        tut_p7_titulo: "Night events",
        tut_p7_texto:  "Every night a real space event happens (solar storm, cosmic rays, dust storm, meteorites...) and takes points from the bars. The Shield blocks 1 point of Life support in radiation events. The next morning a report shows what was lost.",
        tut_p8_titulo: "Daily problems",
        tut_p8_texto:  "From sol 2, problems appear at the start of the day: from the weather (cold, wind, strong storms), from machine maintenance, and from expeditions outside. Choose 1 of 2 options. Nothing is free: every choice has a cost, shown before you choose.",
        tut_p9_titulo: "Expeditions",
        tut_p9_texto:  "Click the airlock door. Every day there are 5 real places explored by NASA's Perseverance rover: 2 low risk (1 action point, 2 kinds of resources), 2 medium risk (2 points, 3 kinds) and 1 high risk (3 points, all 5 kinds). Which resources come is random each day. Cancel is free.",
        tut_p10_titulo: "Controls",
        tut_p10_texto:  "Mouse: click machines and buttons. WASD or arrows: move the camera. Mouse wheel: zoom. Shift + wheel: sideways.",

        // --- Clima de Marte (NASA InSight) e previsão ---
